{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790473641,"nonce":"uZOskHlUwALEMLXKWg5575la7CM=","title":"Library loops over equality, hashing and repr keep calling back after a raise","message":"The stop at the first raising callback (zb_hook_pending) covers map, filter, reduce, min/max and the sorts. Other library loops still call the frontend's hooks after one raised: membership, index, count and remove over dynamic or instance elements (zb_any_eq to zb_hook_instance_eq), list and tuple comparison (zb_any_lt), bisect insort, dict and set lookups hashing or comparing instances (zb_hook_instance_hash/eq), repr/str of a container (zb_hook_instance_repr), and filter's truthiness test of the callback's result. Each runs later callbacks with the error flag set, which ZYNTAX_CHECK_ERROR_FLAG=1 reports when the callee reads the flag.\n\n```python\nclass K:\n    def __eq__(self, other) -\u003e bool:\n        raise ValueError(\"no eq\")\n\ntry:\n    print(K() in [K(), K(), K()])\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(\"ValueError:\", e)\n```\n\nFix: the same `leave_if_pending` after the comparison in each loop whose element kind can call back (`KindOps::calls_back`).","files":null}]}